  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "**This is the easy version of the problem. The only difference is the constraint on AiA_iAi​ — in this version, 1≤Ai≤21 \\leq A_i \\leq 21≤Ai​≤2.**\n\nAn array BBB of length MMM is said to normal if its mean equals its median.\n\nThe mean of BBB is defined to be\n\nB1+B2+…+BMM\\frac{B_1 + B_2 + \\ldots + B_M}{M}MB1​+B2​+…+BM​​For example, the mean of [1,2][1, 2][1,2] is 32=1.5\\frac{3}{2} = 1.523​=1.5, and the mean of [2,2,3,1,3][2, 2, 3, 1, 3][2,2,3,1,3] is 115=2.2\\frac{11}{5} = 2.2511​=2.2.\n\nThe median of BBB is defined to be the element at index ⌈M2⌉\\left\\lceil \\frac{M}{2} \\right\\rceil⌈2M​⌉ when the elements of BBB are **sorted in ascending order**.\n\nThat is, the median of an odd-length array is the middle element after sorting, and the median of an even-length array is the left of the two middle elements after sorting.\n\nFor example, the median of [2,1,2][2, 1, 2][2,1,2] is 222 (sorted order is [1,2,2][1, 2, 2][1,2,2]), and the median of [3,1,2,2,1,1][3, 1, 2, 2, 1, 1][3,1,2,2,1,1] is 111 (sorted order is [1,1,1,2,2,3][1, 1, 1, 2, 2, 3][1,1,1,2,2,3], take the left of the two middle elements which is 111.)\n\nYou're given an array AAA containing NNN integers, **each of which lies between 111 and 222.**\n\nCount the number of contiguous subarrays of AAA that are normal.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the length of the array AAA.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the number of normal subarrays of AAA.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤3⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 3\\cdot 10^51≤N≤3⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤21 \\leq A_i \\leq 21≤Ai​≤2",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 3⋅1053\\cdot 10^53⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
